# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Dependencies
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
node_modules/

# package-lock.json is intentionally NOT ignored — it belongs in the repo.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Build output
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Vite output. Source assets live in app/src, so nothing original is lost here.
app/dist/
dist/
build/
out/
release/
*.tsbuildinfo

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Coordination runtime state
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The SQLite runtime and its JSON mirrors are per-machine live state, not source.
# They churn on every run and the lock file has already caused contention issues.
# This covers the app's own workspace, dev-sandbox/, and any coordinated project
# that happens to live inside the repo.
**/.tiny-agent-office/coordination/runtime.db
**/.tiny-agent-office/coordination/runtime.db-shm
**/.tiny-agent-office/coordination/runtime.db-wal
**/.tiny-agent-office/coordination/runtime.db.lock
**/.tiny-agent-office/coordination/tasks.json
**/.tiny-agent-office/coordination/agents.json
**/.tiny-agent-office/coordination/runs.json
**/.tiny-agent-office/coordination/registry.json
**/.tiny-agent-office/logs/
**/.tiny-agent-office/attachments/

# Kept on purpose: .tiny-agent-office/AGENTS.md, agents-principles.md,
# general-context.md, project.json and daemon-fleet.json are configuration
# and prompt material, not runtime state.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local app state
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Everything in runtime/ is per-machine app state: which projects this user has
# opened, the blueprint tray they keep to hand. None of it is source.
#
# Ignored as a directory rather than file by file, on purpose. The per-file form
# meant every new piece of local state was born untracked-but-not-ignored, and
# stayed that way until somebody remembered to add a line -- a rule that depends
# on memory, and `git add -A` does not wait for memory. Now the default is safe
# and versioning something here takes a deliberate un-ignore below.
runtime/
# Nothing here yet. Un-ignore explicitly if runtime/ ever holds real source:
# !runtime/something-that-belongs-in-git.json

# PIDs of the dev launcher and its children. Live state for this machine only.
runtime/dev-processes.json

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Logs and diagnostics
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.log
npm-debug.log*
logs/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Environment and secrets
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Editor and OS
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
!.vscode/launch.json
.idea/
*.swp
Thumbs.db
Desktop.ini
$RECYCLE.BIN/
.DS_Store

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Project-local development material
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# These folders contain machine-local coordination state, design experiments,
# handoff notes, and scratch projects. None of them belongs in a public release.
/.tiny-agent-office/
/TEMP/
/ERASEME/
/dev-sandbox/
/TrabajoBlackBoxBirdTestApp3/
/newUIPlan.md
/docs/reference/
